{
  "$schema": "https://pmef.net/schemas/0.9/pmef-catalog.schema.json",
  "catalogId": "profiles-aisc-extended",
  "catalogType": "STEEL_PROFILES",
  "standard": "AISC Steel Construction Manual, 16th Edition",
  "version": "2024.3",
  "description": "Extended AISC structural steel sections: American Standard Channels (C), Miscellaneous Channels (MC), and Structural Tees cut from W-shapes (WT). Complements the main profiles-aisc.json catalog.",
  "families": {
    "C": "American Standard Channel (ASTM A36/A572)",
    "MC": "Miscellaneous Channel (ASTM A36/A572)",
    "WT": "Structural Tee cut from W-shape (ASTM A992/A572)"
  },
  "units": {
    "length": "in (dimensions also in mm: d_mm, bf_mm, tw_mm, tf_mm)",
    "area": "in2",
    "second_moment": "in4",
    "section_modulus": "in3",
    "mass_per_length": "lb/ft"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Version 2024.3 adds d_mm, bf_mm, tw_mm and tf_mm (inch value × 25.4, rounded half-up to 0.1 mm) so that unit-neutral consumers such as catalog snapping (pmef-snap/2, RFC-0011) can read C and MC channels. Inch values are unchanged and remain authoritative.",
    "Version 2024.2 aligns C, MC and WT entries with the AISC Shapes Database v16.0 (WT Ix/Sx were about half the AISC values). Removed WT18x150 (not an AISC designation; the nearest section is WT18x151). Checked with scripts/check-catalogs.py.",
    "All section properties from AISC Steel Construction Manual, 16th Edition.",
    "C-shapes per ASTM A6/A6M. WT-shapes are halves of corresponding W-shapes.",
    "This catalog is not a substitute for the official published standards."
  ],
